  "title": "Bases of many weights",
  "statement": {
    "representation": "markdown-latex",
    "text": "Let $G$ be an (additive) abelian group, and for every $S \\subseteq G$ let ${\\mathit stab}(S) = \\{ g \\in G: g + S = S \\}$.\n\nConjecture Let $M$ be a matroid on $E$, let $w: E \\rightarrow G$ be a map, put $S = \\{ \\sum_{b \\in B} w(b): B \\mbox{ is a base} \\}$ and $H = {\\mathit stab}(S)$. Then $$|S| \\ge |H| \\left( 1 - rk(M) + \\sum_{Q \\in G/H} rk(w^{-1}(Q)) \\right).$$",
